{
  "abstract": "A machine-checked proof of the Lie-Trotter product formula in an arbitrary complete normed algebra over the reals with norm-one unit, with a commutator-scaling error bound: for all A, B and n >= 1, the distance from (exp(A/n) exp(B/n))^n to exp(A + B) is at most ‖AB - BA‖ / (2n) · e^(‖A‖ + ‖B‖).",
