      {
        "identifier": "https://github.com/zblore/csd-lean4/blob/0fd97c69e26a9e2e31c4313b1c8f3dce10ef20fb/CsdLean4/Mathlib/Analysis/NormedSpace/TrotterGeneral.lean",
        "note": "My larger Lean project, where this proof was added on 20 August 2026 (commit 0fd97c69). The extraction replaced that file's import of a csd-lean4 staging module, which it did not use, with direct Mathlib imports; changed the namespace to LieTrotter; exposed the explicit bound, already a step inside the original convergence proof, as its own theorem; and ported the file to Lean v4.35.0-rc3.",
        "relationship": "builds-on"
      },
      {
        "identifier": "https://github.com/PerAlexandersson/RealRooted/blob/ee8e64ae28f8554194167669b357f6235ba2a104/RealRooted/Mathlib/Analysis/Normed/Operator/Trotter.lean",
        "note": "ContinuousLinearMap.tendsto_exp_add_trotter, added 16 October 2026: operator-norm convergence for bounded real-linear endomorphisms of a Banach space, with an arbitrary real time and exponent n + 1, and helper lemmas for any complete normed real algebra with ‖1‖ ≤ 1. Its convergence statement and the one here are equivalent (a Banach algebra with norm-one unit embeds isometrically in its bounded operators); it also covers the zero space. Its proof uses the same four-term decomposition and contains an explicit bound internally, not scaling with the commutator. The contribution here is the commutator-scaling bound as a stated theorem. The csd-lean4 proof this repository extracts dates from 20 August 2026. RealRooted's source credits Aristotle.",
        "relationship": "independent"
      },
      {
        "identifier": "https://github.com/zblore/csd-lean4/blob/38641a078ec5a42aa26707e6ed80341294ed26cb/CsdLean4/Mathlib/Analysis/Matrix/TrotterProduct.lean",
        "note": "My earlier proof of the formula for skew-Hermitian complex matrices (trotter_skew, 9 August 2026), which the Banach-algebra proof generalises.",
        "relationship": "builds-on"
      },
      {
        "identifier": "https://github.com/TauCetiProject/TauCeti/blob/0643ddb4969043b9306a0da476f5f5bec7763476/TauCeti/Geometry/Lie/Exponential/Trotter.lean",
        "note": "A product formula for finite-dimensional real Lie groups, added 15 August 2026. A different generalisation of the matrix formula, through Lie-group exponentials.",
        "relationship": "independent"
      },
      {
        "identifier": "https://github.com/QudeLeap/Lean-QuantumAlg/blob/971dc8be8a153a116b6d7cd748f984d545861b00/QuantumAlg/Analysis/Trotter/FirstOrder.lean",
        "note": "First-order operator-norm Trotter error bounds for finite-dimensional Hamiltonians, including commutator-sensitive bounds. Related, for quantum simulation.",
